\name{cellucid_field_consensus}
\alias{cellucid_field_consensus}
\title{Build the consensus column}
\usage{
cellucid_field_consensus(viewer, key, field, mapping, settings, provenance)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{key}{The consensus column's name. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{field}{The annotated column the consensus is of. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The column name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{Categories belong to columns of the cells. Exactly \code{"obs"}. Required.}}}
\item{mapping}{The outcome of each category of the column (a category left out is pending). A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Required.}
\item{settings}{The consensus rule it was built with. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{minAnnotators}}{Voters a category needs before it can agree. A whole number (at least 0). Required.}\item{\code{threshold}}{The net share of votes the leading label needs (-1 to 1). A number (at least -1, at most 1). Required.}}}
\item{provenance}{Where the votes came from. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{branch}}{Its branch, when known. Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{commit}}{The commit pulled, when known. Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{pulledAt}}{When it was last pulled (ISO 8601), null when never. Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{repository}}{The GitHub repository (owner/name), null when none was connected. Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Required.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
The community annotation's consensus for a categorical column as a column of its own: each cell gets the agreed label of its category, or the status of a category without one (disputed, pending); built again under the same name, it is replaced. The outcome of each category is named in the parameters, so it replays by name on any dataset with the same column and categories.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.consensus} (Fields). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{field-overlays}, \code{active-field}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_field_consensus(viewer, field = list(key = "cell_type",
      source = "obs"), key = "x", mapping = list(list(category = "T cells",
      label = "x", status = "consensus", voters = 0)),
      provenance = list(branch = "x", commit = "x", pulledAt = "x",
          repository = "x"), settings = list(minAnnotators = 0,
          threshold = -1))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
